00:01:12.590 --> 00:01:15.880
It happens especially when
I'm laying down in bed.

00:01:15.880 --> 00:01:18.850
Monica, that sounds like
a very unique symptom.

00:01:18.850 --> 00:01:21.000
When things are going numb in your body,

00:01:21.000 --> 00:01:22.090
two things are happening.

00:01:22.090 --> 00:01:25.060
Most likely something's
happening with the nerves.

00:01:25.060 --> 00:01:28.040
So is there pressure
being put on the nerves

00:01:28.040 --> 00:01:29.830
that's causing them to malfunction

00:01:29.830 --> 00:01:31.640
and causing you to feel numbness?

00:01:31.640 --> 00:01:33.930
Also it could be a lack of blood flow,

00:01:33.930 --> 00:01:36.330
for example, if you cut off the
circulation to your fingers,

00:01:36.330 --> 00:01:37.500
your fingers can go numb.

00:01:37.500 --> 00:01:40.470
Which one of those two things
can be happening to you

00:01:40.470 --> 00:01:41.950
is an important question.

00:01:41.950 --> 00:01:45.230
It can be answered only
through a thorough history,

00:01:45.230 --> 00:01:46.970
a thorough physical exam and again,

00:01:46.970 --> 00:01:49.170
maybe some tests or labs
that need to be ordered.

00:01:49.170 --> 00:01:51.140
Go see your doctor.

