00:03:11.310 --> 00:03:13.020
Kaylor Andrews hey doctor Mike,

00:03:13.020 --> 00:03:15.710
I was wondering what are the
white dots on fingernails,

00:03:15.710 --> 00:03:18.500
I've heard lots of
different reasons as to why.

00:03:18.500 --> 00:03:21.710
Leukonychia, specifically
punctate Leukonychia

00:03:21.710 --> 00:03:24.160
is white dots on nails

00:03:24.160 --> 00:03:25.810
and specifically white dots

00:03:25.810 --> 00:03:28.480
that when you press on your
nail bed they don't disappear.

00:03:28.480 --> 00:03:31.090
A lot of times this happens
as a result of trauma,

00:03:31.090 --> 00:03:32.300
like you bang your nail

00:03:32.300 --> 00:03:33.810
and you get a little white spot on it.

00:03:33.810 --> 00:03:36.880
If you have a lot of these
and on multiple fingers,

00:03:36.880 --> 00:03:39.818
even if as far as you
find lines on your nails,

00:03:39.818 --> 00:03:41.740
that's something you should bring up

00:03:41.740 --> 00:03:43.840
to your doctor, especially if they're new

00:03:43.840 --> 00:03:46.730
or enlarging or increasing in number,

00:03:46.730 --> 00:03:48.760
because the state of your nails

00:03:48.760 --> 00:03:51.230
tell a great story about
the status of your health.

00:03:51.230 --> 00:03:53.380
Those who have immune problems,

00:03:53.380 --> 00:03:55.650
pulmonary problems, cardiac problems,

00:03:55.650 --> 00:03:58.430
we see certain signs inside fingernails

00:03:58.430 --> 00:04:01.570
that can give us and point
us as to where we should look

00:04:01.570 --> 00:04:02.650
inside their body.

00:04:02.650 --> 00:04:05.830
Every good doctor looks at patients' nails

00:04:05.830 --> 00:04:07.200
when we're doing a physical exam.

