I need to do a physical exam

00:05:52.639 --> 00:05:54.410
I may need to order lab work,

00:05:54.410 --> 00:05:56.600
maybe do some kind of culture,

00:05:56.600 --> 00:05:58.160
to see what bacteria's around,

00:05:58.160 --> 00:06:00.620
but I'll talk about my past experiences.

00:06:00.620 --> 00:06:01.890
I've had a lot of patients come in

00:06:01.890 --> 00:06:04.860
with the misconception that
they have some sort of bug,

00:06:04.860 --> 00:06:06.090
whether that's viral or bacterial,

00:06:06.090 --> 00:06:07.900
it doesn't matter for this explanation.

00:06:07.900 --> 00:06:09.710
The reason they think that is
cause they have a sore throat

00:06:09.710 --> 00:06:11.620
just like you're saying for
an extended period of time.

00:06:11.620 --> 00:06:13.060
So I ask a bunch of questions

00:06:13.060 --> 00:06:15.100
and what we end up finding
out is that they have

00:06:15.100 --> 00:06:16.980
post-nasal drip, which means that you have

00:06:16.980 --> 00:06:19.760
excess mucus production
from the posterior part

00:06:19.760 --> 00:06:21.320
of your nose that at night,

00:06:21.320 --> 00:06:22.890
especially when you're lying down

00:06:22.890 --> 00:06:24.530
drips onto the back of your throat,

00:06:24.530 --> 00:06:27.400
your pharynx and it causes soreness,

00:06:27.400 --> 00:06:29.980
because that mucus is irritating
the back of your throat.

00:06:29.980 --> 00:06:31.530
Another thing that could be going on

00:06:31.530 --> 00:06:35.244
is something called LPR,
laryngopharyngeal reflux.

00:06:35.244 --> 00:06:36.890
I know that's a mouthful,

00:06:36.890 --> 00:06:41.080
but all that is is it's
traditional heartburn acid reflux,

00:06:41.080 --> 00:06:43.040
the acid from your stomach going up,

00:06:43.040 --> 00:06:44.760
but it's not causing you burning here.

00:06:44.760 --> 00:06:47.700
To cause burning here it takes
a substantial amount of acid

00:06:47.700 --> 00:06:50.690
but now if a small amount
of acid touches the back

00:06:50.690 --> 00:06:52.500
of your throat that can cause damage

00:06:52.500 --> 00:06:54.370
that can last many weeks

00:06:54.370 --> 00:06:56.040
and if you're eating citrusy foods

00:06:56.040 --> 00:06:58.620
or you're consistently
getting this acid in there,

00:06:58.620 --> 00:07:00.330
you're causing repetitive damage

00:07:00.330 --> 00:07:01.980
and that can cause a chronic sore throat.

00:07:01.980 --> 00:07:03.810
Every once in a great while

00:07:03.810 --> 00:07:05.430
I feel a sharp pain in my chest

00:07:05.430 --> 00:07:07.090
or my side when I breath in

00:07:07.090 --> 00:07:09.570
which causes shortness of
breath for like two minutes.

