Is this normal?

00:07:10.450 --> 00:07:12.850
Jaybirdie, this doesn't sound normal.

00:07:12.850 --> 00:07:16.250
Any time you're feeling
symptoms in your chest

00:07:16.250 --> 00:07:19.806
or your lungs that induce
shortness of breath,

00:07:19.806 --> 00:07:21.620
that should be checked out.

00:07:21.620 --> 00:07:24.590
I don't know your age, but
odds are you're probably young

00:07:24.590 --> 00:07:26.338
and you don't have heart disease,

00:07:26.338 --> 00:07:29.850
but even though something
has a lower likelihood

00:07:29.850 --> 00:07:31.500
of occurring in your age group,

00:07:31.500 --> 00:07:34.900
if that one thing can be very
dangerous to your health,

00:07:34.900 --> 00:07:37.230
like a heart attach,
you wanna catch early.

00:07:37.230 --> 00:07:39.310
My thoughts if I had to venture and guess

00:07:39.310 --> 00:07:41.070
and this is not a medical opinion,

00:07:41.070 --> 00:07:43.030
my medical opinion is that
you should see your doctor,

00:07:43.030 --> 00:07:44.820
but somethings that could be going on is

00:07:44.820 --> 00:07:47.160
that you can have a muscle cramp

00:07:47.160 --> 00:07:48.850
within the inner coastal muscles,

00:07:48.850 --> 00:07:51.002
which is the muscles in between your ribs

00:07:51.002 --> 00:07:53.796
and when you get that
sort of spasm in there

00:07:53.796 --> 00:07:55.290
it can make it heard to breathe

00:07:55.290 --> 00:07:56.840
'cause you can't take a deep breath

00:07:56.840 --> 00:07:58.580
and maybe that's what you're feeling.

00:07:58.580 --> 00:08:01.920
Also I've heard of people
having a diaphragm cramp

00:08:01.920 --> 00:08:05.010
which is that large muscle
immediately below your lungs

00:08:05.010 --> 00:08:08.060
that you can also have a
cramp or some kind of pain in

00:08:08.060 --> 00:08:10.170
and that can also make it
difficult for you to breathe.

