00:08:24.810 --> 00:08:27.720
Riley to answer your
question very simply, yes.

00:08:27.720 --> 00:08:30.280
A headache that's that
severe or that chronic,

00:08:30.280 --> 00:08:32.130
meaning it's going on
for a long period of time

00:08:32.130 --> 00:08:33.920
should be evaluated by a doctor.

00:08:33.920 --> 00:08:36.530
Does that mean that there's
something worrisome going on?

00:08:36.530 --> 00:08:37.480
Not necessarily.

00:08:37.480 --> 00:08:39.440
There are some red flags that we look for

00:08:39.440 --> 00:08:40.760
in patients who have headaches

00:08:40.760 --> 00:08:42.840
and don't panic if you have some of these.

00:08:42.840 --> 00:08:44.600
These are just some red flags.

00:08:44.600 --> 00:08:47.080
A, you wake up with a headache.

00:08:47.080 --> 00:08:49.340
B, you have a headache
with physical exertion

00:08:49.340 --> 00:08:50.440
or sexual activity.

00:08:50.440 --> 00:08:53.510
C, you get headaches after you eat food.

00:08:53.510 --> 00:08:57.300
D, you have a headache that
causes neurological symptoms.

00:08:57.300 --> 00:08:59.610
Numbness of your face, bad vision

00:08:59.610 --> 00:09:01.100
and this can happen with migraines,

00:09:01.100 --> 00:09:02.810
but it is a red flag that we look at.

00:09:02.810 --> 00:09:05.960
The final one I guess would
be that you have a headache

00:09:05.960 --> 00:09:07.610
that's very severe that's been ongoing

00:09:07.610 --> 00:09:09.220
for an extended period of time.

00:09:09.220 --> 00:09:10.740
Now I now that's not complete,

